    "note": "Farlow, whose large hands earned him the nickname 'the Octopus', had what Stuart Nicholson calls a very personal way of using large intervals, and he strung chains of arpeggios together to contrast his single-note lines. This phrase borrows the wide-interval arpeggio and the arpeggio chain, in a version that fits a normal hand."
